<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 29 August, from 708 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">708 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,318 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Empress Genmei orders the Wadōkaichin, Japan's oldest official coinage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Wadōkaichin, the oldest official Japanese coinage, was first recorded on the order of Empress Genmei. Long thought to be the first coins made in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, they were in fact preceded by the Fuhon-sen, manufactured from 683.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/870">870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Aghlabids take Melite, ending Byzantine rule in Malta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege, Melite, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>, the last island around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in Byzantine hands, fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabids</a>, reinforced by a fleet sent from Sicily. The town was plundered and its fortifications razed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabid dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1219">1219 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">807 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ayyubid Egypt defeats the army of the Fifth Crusade at Fariskur</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Outside the Ayyubid camp at Fariskur, the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a> fought a pitched battle with Ayyubid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> while its siege of Damietta was still under way. The Ayyubid victory had little effect on the course of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1350">1350 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">676 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III defeats a Castilian fleet off Winchelsea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, an English fleet of 50 ships under King Edward III defeated a Castilian fleet of 47 larger vessels commanded by Charles de la Cerda. Between 14 and 26 Castilian ships were captured and several sunk.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1526">1526 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">500 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suleiman the Magnificent crushes Hungary at Mohács</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ottoman army destroyed the Hungarian forces at Mohács; King Louis II drowned while fleeing. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was partitioned, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> inherited its crown.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1842">1842 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">184 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Nanking ends the First Opium War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong-island">Hong Kong Island</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, opened five ports to foreign trade and paid a large indemnity. It was the first of the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unequal-treaties">unequal treaties</a>' China remembers as a century of humiliation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1949">1949 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">77 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union tests its first atomic bomb</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The USSR exploded its first atomic bomb at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semey">Semipalatinsk</a> in Kazakhstan, years earlier than the West expected. The American nuclear monopoly was over and the arms race had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Beatles play their last concert for paying fans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-beatles">The Beatles</a> played a half-hour set at Candlestick Park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>. They then gave up touring to concentrate on studio albums such as Sgt. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">Pepper</a>'s Lonely Hearts Club Band.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">Pepper</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2005">2005 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">21 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hurricane Katrina strikes the US Gulf Coast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Katrina made landfall as a Category 3 hurricane; storm surge broke the levees of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> and flooded some 80 per cent of the city. More than 1,300 people died and the government response was widely condemned.</p></div></li></ol>
